IMPORT prelude

-- Antitrust Guidelines for Business Activities Affecting Workers (U.S. Department of
-- Justice and Federal Trade Commission, revised January 2025) -- THE NOUNS.
--
-- AGENCY ENFORCEMENT POLICY, NOT LAW. n.1 [pdf page 2]: the document "has no force or
-- effect of law", is "not intended to create any substantive or procedural rights
-- enforceable at law by any party", and does not limit the agencies' discretion. Nothing
-- here says what a court must hold.
--
-- Types only: no rules, no #EVAL. Every field is a fact or a finding the caller
-- supplies; findings are never computed from other fields, and each says so. A field
-- that no rule reads is kept so that a fixture can show the text's "even if" or "need
-- not": it is marked "not read". A BOOLEAN finding is named as the positive finding, and
-- FALSE means only that the finding has not been made; where the text distinguishes
-- "not yet determined" from "found not", the input has a value for each. There are no
-- numeric inputs.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/2025-business-activities-affecting-workers-guidelines.txt.
-- Section numbers are as printed; "[pdf page N]" is the page marker of that text.

§ `Antitrust Guidelines for Business Activities Affecting Workers (2025) -- the nouns`

§§ `Overview: the list of agreements and practices`

-- Overview [pdf page 3]: "Examples of such agreements include:" five numbered items,
-- then "This list is not exhaustive." The last value is a practice the list does not
-- name (fork F3).
DECLARE `Practice in the Overview's list` IS ONE OF
    `item 1: an agreement between companies not to recruit, solicit, or hire workers, or to fix wages or terms of employment`
    `item 2: an agreement in the franchise context not to poach, hire, or solicit employees of the franchisor or franchisees`
    `item 3: an exchange of competitively sensitive information with companies that compete for workers`
    `item 4: an employment agreement that restricts workers' freedom to leave their job`
    `item 5: another restrictive, exclusionary, or predatory employment condition that harms competition`
    `an agreement or business practice the list does not name`

§§ `General principles: the businesses`

-- General principles [pdf page 4]: "Businesses can compete to hire or retain workers even
-- if they make different products or offer different services." A labor market is the
-- caller's delineation, named by a STRING; the guidelines give no test for drawing one
-- (fork F1). The products and services are not read by any rule.
DECLARE `Business` HAS
    `the name of the business` IS A STRING
    `the labor markets in which it hires or retains workers` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the products or services it makes, sells or provides` IS A LIST OF STRING      -- not read

-- Two participants in a potential agreement or exchange.
DECLARE `Two businesses` HAS
    `one business` IS A `Business`
    `the other business` IS A `Business`
    `the businesses are potentially competing employers` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- 1 [pdf page 6]: "competing or potentially competing employers"; a finding the text does not define
    `they have some other collaborative or cooperative relationship, such as a joint venture` IS A BOOLEAN  -- General principles [pdf page 4]; not read

§§ `General principles: the agreement`

-- General principles [pdf pages 3-4]: the agencies "will focus on whether there is an
-- agreement between businesses", and consider direct and circumstantial evidence of one.
-- Whether there is an agreement is the caller's finding, never inferred from the
-- evidence (fork F2); the three values keep "found none" apart from "not determined".
DECLARE `Finding on whether there is an agreement` IS ONE OF
    `the agencies identify an agreement between the businesses`
    `the agencies find no agreement between the businesses`
    `whether there is an agreement has not been determined`

-- General principles [pdf pages 3-4] and 1 [pdf pages 5-6]: none of these is read by any
-- rule. An agreement "need not be explicit or written down", can be "formal or informal;
-- express or implicit", "need not be written down or talked about at all", and such
-- agreements are illegal "even if they are never carried out"; section 1 adds "between
-- individuals at different businesses", "directly or through an intermediary", and "even
-- if they did not result in actual harm such as lower wages".
DECLARE `Form of the agreement` HAS
    `it is formal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is express` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is written down` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was spoken or talked about` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was ever carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was made by individuals at the businesses rather than by the businesses themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was entered into through an intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it resulted in actual harm such as lower wages` IS A BOOLEAN

-- General principles [pdf page 4]: "For example, they may consider whether a business
-- has ...". The four named kinds, and anything else the caller offers as direct or
-- circumstantial evidence (the list is an example, so it is open: fork F3).
DECLARE `Evidence of an agreement` HAS
    `a business has discussed with another company wages or other potential terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a business has engaged in parallel behavior that demonstrates a shared understanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a business has invited another company to participate in a plan to restrict competition for workers, followed by action consistent with that plan` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a business has used a common intermediary to obtain competitively sensitive information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other direct or circumstantial evidence offered` IS A LIST OF STRING

§§ `Sections 1, 2 and 6: what the businesses agree`

-- 1 [pdf pages 5-6] and n.11 [pdf page 5]: the terms section 1 names, in substance
-- rather than form. One term per agreement; an agreement with several terms is read term
-- by term (fork F8).
DECLARE `What the businesses agree` IS ONE OF
    `to fix workers' salaries or other terms of compensation or employment, such as bonuses or benefits, at a specific level or within a range`
    `to align, stabilize, or otherwise coordinate the wages they set, as by a range, ceiling, or benchmark for calculating wages, without agreeing on a specific wage`
    `to set a starting point for compensation`
    `not to recruit, solicit, hire, or otherwise compete for current, former, or potential workers`
    `to restrict a company's ability to hire another company's workers, without completely prohibiting it`
    `not to cold call workers`
    `to request permission from the other company before trying to hire an employee`
    `something else relating to workers`

-- 2 [pdf pages 6-7].
DECLARE `Franchise relationship of the parties` IS ONE OF
    `a franchisor and its franchisee`
    `franchisees of the same franchisor`
    `no franchise relationship`

-- 6 [pdf page 11]: "workers, which includes both employees and independent contractors".
DECLARE `Kind of workers concerned` IS ONE OF
    `employees`
    `independent contractors`
    `both employees and independent contractors`

-- An agreement between businesses relating to workers, as sections 1, 2 and 6 and the
-- general principles read it.
DECLARE `Agreement between businesses relating to workers` HAS
    `the finding on whether there is an agreement` IS A `Finding on whether there is an agreement`
    `the businesses` IS A `Two businesses`
    `what the businesses agree` IS A `What the businesses agree`
    `the firms remain allowed to hire workers who apply for a position without first being solicited` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 1 [pdf page 6], for a no-cold-call agreement; not read
    `the workers concerned` IS A `Kind of workers concerned`                                                       -- 6 [pdf page 11]
    `the businesses are platforms through which the independent contractors offer their services` IS A BOOLEAN      -- 6 [pdf page 11]
    `the franchise relationship of the parties` IS A `Franchise relationship of the parties`                       -- 2 [pdf pages 6-7]
    `the franchisor organizes or enforces the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN                                              -- 2 [pdf page 7]; read for an agreement among franchisees
    `the restraint is subordinate and collateral to a broader business collaboration, such as a joint venture` IS A BOOLEAN   -- n.15 [pdf page 6], a finding
    `the restraint is reasonably necessary to achieve the procompetitive potential of that collaboration` IS A BOOLEAN       -- n.15 [pdf page 6], a finding
    `the form of the agreement` IS A `Form of the agreement`                                                       -- not read

§§ `Section 1: a report of an antitrust crime`

-- 1 [pdf page 6]: the Criminal Antitrust Anti-Retaliation Act "provides whistleblower
-- protections for employees, contractors, subcontractors, and agents who report antitrust
-- crimes, including no-poach and wage-fixing agreements".
DECLARE `Role of the person reporting` IS ONE OF
    `an employee`
    `a contractor`
    `a subcontractor`
    `an agent`
    `another person`

DECLARE `What the person reports` IS ONE OF
    `a no-poach agreement`
    `a wage-fixing agreement`
    `another antitrust crime`
    `conduct that is not an antitrust crime`

DECLARE `Report of an antitrust crime` HAS
    `the role of the person reporting` IS A `Role of the person reporting`
    `what the person reports` IS A `What the person reports`

§§ `Section 3: an exchange of information`

-- 3 [pdf pages 7-8]: the routes the text names.
DECLARE `How the information is shared` IS ONE OF
    `directly between the businesses`
    `through a third party or intermediary`
    `through an algorithm or other software, or through a third party's tool or product`

-- 3 [pdf page 7]: "has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect". Three values:
-- the text's condition found, its contrary found, and no assessment yet (fork F12).
DECLARE `Finding on the exchange's effect` IS ONE OF
    `the exchange has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`
    `the exchange neither has nor is likely to have an anticompetitive effect`
    `the exchange's effect has not been assessed`

DECLARE `Information exchange` HAS
    `the businesses` IS A `Two businesses`
    `the information is competitively sensitive information about compensation or other terms or conditions of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the information is shared` IS A `How the information is shared`
    `the exchange is explicit rather than implied from the conduct of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- 3 [pdf page 7]; not read
    `the finding on the exchange's effect` IS A `Finding on the exchange's effect`
    `the effect was intended` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                                     -- 3 [pdf page 7]: "whether or not that effect was intended"; not read
    `the exchange is used to generate wage or other benefit recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN                                      -- 3 [pdf page 7]
    `the exchange requires the businesses to strictly adhere to the recommendations` IS A BOOLEAN                              -- 3 [pdf page 7]; not read
    `the businesses agree to use shared wage recommendations, lists, calculations, or algorithms` IS A BOOLEAN                 -- 3 [pdf page 8], a finding
    `the participants retain some discretion or cheat on the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN                                           -- 3 [pdf page 8]; not read
    `the businesses agree to share information about wages or other terms of employment` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- 3 [pdf page 8], a finding
    `the businesses are parties to a legitimate transaction or a joint venture or other collaborative activity` IS A BOOLEAN   -- 3 [pdf page 8]; not read

§§ `Sections 4 and 5: an employment term`

-- 4 [pdf page 8] and the bullets of 5 [pdf page 10]. The kind is the caller's: a provision
-- requiring a penalty on leaving is a non-compete provision in Overview item 4 and an
-- exit fee in section 5 (fork F15).
DECLARE `Kind of employment term` IS ONE OF
    `a non-compete clause`
    `a non-disclosure agreement`
    `a training repayment agreement provision`
    `a non-solicitation agreement that prohibits the worker from soliciting former clients or customers of the employer`
    `an exit fee or liquidated damages provision`
    `another restrictive, exclusionary, or predatory employment condition`

-- Every BOOLEAN after the kind is a finding the caller supplies, and FALSE means only that
-- it has not been made: the text attaches no statement to its contrary.
DECLARE `Employment term` HAS
    `the kind of term` IS A `Kind of employment term`
    `it restricts the worker from switching jobs` IS A BOOLEAN                                                    -- 4 [pdf page 8]
    `it restricts the worker from starting a competing business` IS A BOOLEAN                                     -- 4 [pdf page 8]
    `it limits competition` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                          -- 4 [pdf page 8]: "restraints on worker mobility that limit competition"
    `it functions to prevent the worker from seeking, accepting or working in another job, or from starting a business` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 5 [pdf page 10], the four bullets (fork F16)
    `it prohibits disclosure of any information that is usable in or relates to an industry` IS A BOOLEAN        -- 5 [pdf page 10], a non-disclosure agreement
    `it is worded so broadly as to suggest that workers who report potential violations of law, or who cooperate with a government investigation, could face lawsuits and adverse employment consequences` IS A BOOLEAN  -- 5 [pdf page 10]
    `it impedes worker mobility or otherwise undermines competition` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- 5 [pdf page 10]
    `there are indications that it is harming competition` IS A BOOLEAN                                          -- 5 [pdf page 11]

§§ `Section 7: a claim about earnings`

-- 7 [pdf page 12]: "false or misleading claims about potential earnings that workers
-- (including both employees and independent contractors) may realize".
DECLARE `Claim about workers' potential earnings` HAS
    `the claim is false` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- a finding
    `the claim is misleading` IS A BOOLEAN                  -- a finding
    `the workers concerned` IS A `Kind of workers concerned` -- not read
